# SDK Refork: Rebuild from paas_customer, targeting Supacharge next

## Context and why

The current SDK set was extracted from `paas_customer` (the original Foodyman customer app,
also merged with `paas_driver`/`paas_manager` into `RokctApp/lib_backup` at one point) years ago,
but the extraction was never finished. An audit found `core_sdk` alone has 242 unique imported
paths across the workspace, of which only 40 actually resolve — 202 are "phantom" imports that
were rewritten to point at `core_sdk/src/...` locations that were never actually populated. A
sample check found phantom paths match `paas_customer/lib/...` (with the `src/` prefix stripped)
at a 100% rate. This is not a few bugs — the foundation itself doesn't contain most of what
consumers assume it contains.

Decision: rather than patch this, rebuild from `paas_customer` as the real source of truth,
**moving** files into their correct new SDK homes (not copying) — `paas_customer/lib/` should
end up thin after this, since its content has actually relocated, not been duplicated.

**Sequencing — this matters, do not deviate**: work on `paas_customer` only in this pass. Do
**not** touch `paas_driver` or `paas_manager` — attempting all three risks running out of budget
before reaching the actual priority, which is getting Supacharge built on the new SDK set. Once
`paas_customer`'s SDKs are extracted and `paas_customer` itself builds and runs correctly against
them, stop and report — the next phase (building Supacharge on this foundation) is a separate,
later task.

Also **disregard `paas_customer/frappe/` backend code entirely** in this pass — Dart/Flutter
extraction only.

